      "content": "The debate over school vouchers revolves around the idea of providing students with public funds to attend private schools, often termed as \"educational choice.\" Proponents argue that vouchers help low-income students access better educational opportunities by allowing them to escape underfunded public schools and attend higher-performing private institutions. Critics, on the other hand, claim that vouchers divert funds away from public schools, exacerbating existing inequalities and undermining the public education system's effectiveness. Additionally, some argue that voucher programs can create segregation and weaken public schools, as only those with significant financial resources can access these alternative options.",
