      "content": "Critics of school vouchers often focus on concerns beyond just the monetary aspect. Some argue that vouchers can lead to privatization and commodification of education, where schools are prioritized for profit rather than the needs of their students. Others worry that vouchers ease segregation, potentially harming students of color and low-income students who may be kept in underfunded schools in order to help more affluent students access better options. Additionally, many critics view vouchers as a thinly veiled attempt to dismantle public education funding systems and their existing arrangements.",
