      "content": "i get that, but it seems like the 'dismantling' thing is a bit of a stretch. most people just want to give parents a choice, right? it feels like the critics are being really pessimistic/negative about just wanting kids to have better schools. don't you think the benefits of choice usually outweigh these systemic fears?",
